# File: specs/feature-add-github-actions-contribution-gates-to-project-setup/feature.gherkin
# Generated from: specs/feature-add-github-actions-contribution-gates-to-project-setup/requirements.md
# Issue: #125

Feature: Add GitHub Actions contribution gates to project setup
  As a project maintainer using nmg-sdlc-managed repositories
  I want project setup and upgrade flows to install a GitHub Actions PR contribution gate and richer contribution guidance
  So that pull requests that bypass nmg-sdlc expectations are blocked before merge with actionable feedback

  Scenario: Init creates the managed PR gate
    Given a project runs "$nmg-sdlc:init-config"
    And ".github/workflows/nmg-sdlc-contribution-gate.yml" is absent or already nmg-sdlc-managed
    When runner config setup completes
    Then ".github/workflows/nmg-sdlc-contribution-gate.yml" exists
    And the workflow contains the current nmg-sdlc managed marker and managed-version metadata
    And the workflow validates pull requests against nmg-sdlc contribution expectations

  Scenario: Upgrade reconciles missing or outdated gates
    Given an initialized project is missing the contribution-gate workflow or has an older nmg-sdlc-managed version
    When "$nmg-sdlc:upgrade-project" runs
    Then the workflow is reported as a managed non-destructive upgrade finding
    And applying the finding creates or updates only the managed nmg-sdlc workflow
    And unrelated project files and unmanaged workflows are preserved

  Scenario: Non-compliant PRs fail with actionable output
    Given a pull request lacks required nmg-sdlc contribution evidence
    When the generated contribution-gate workflow runs
    Then CI fails
    And the output names each missing expectation
    And the output points contributors to "CONTRIBUTING.md" or the relevant nmg-sdlc artifact path

  Scenario: Existing GitHub Actions are preserved
    Given a project already has unrelated workflows under ".github/workflows/"
    When "$nmg-sdlc:init-config" or "$nmg-sdlc:upgrade-project" manages the contribution gate
    Then unrelated workflows are not overwritten, moved, deleted, or reformatted
    And only ".github/workflows/nmg-sdlc-contribution-gate.yml" is created or reconciled when that path is nmg-sdlc-owned

  Scenario: CONTRIBUTING.md becomes a north star for non-plugin contributors
    Given a developer does not have nmg-sdlc installed locally
    When they read generated or updated "CONTRIBUTING.md"
    Then they can understand expected issue quality
    And they can understand spec location and steering alignment
    And they can understand implementation scope, verification evidence, PR readiness, and contribution-gate failure remediation

  Scenario: Workflow security and portability hold
    Given the generated workflow runs on pull requests
    When it evaluates repository content and PR metadata
    Then it uses minimal GitHub token permissions
    And it requires no repository secrets by default
    And it does not run untrusted PR content as code
    And it remains stack-agnostic unless a project explicitly declares additional steering-level verification expectations

  Scenario: Path collisions are safe
    Given ".github/workflows/nmg-sdlc-contribution-gate.yml" exists without the nmg-sdlc managed marker
    When "$nmg-sdlc:init-config" or "$nmg-sdlc:upgrade-project" reaches the contribution-gate step
    Then the workflow is not overwritten
    And the skill records a gap naming the occupied path and required manual remediation
    And unattended mode does not prompt or force the replacement

  Scenario: Gate installation is idempotent
    Given the managed contribution-gate workflow and guide content are already current
    When "$nmg-sdlc:init-config" or "$nmg-sdlc:upgrade-project" runs again
    Then no duplicate workflow content is produced
    And no duplicate README links or contribution-guide sections are produced
    And no unrelated diffs are produced
    And the skill summary reports the gate as already present

  # Added by issue #143
  Scenario: Issue and spec references are cross-checked
    Given a pull request references issue "#N" and includes or links a spec directory
    When the contribution gate evaluates the pull request and bounded artifacts in that spec directory
    Then at least one selected spec artifact references the same issue number
    And an unrelated issue number appearing only in the pull request or another spec does not satisfy the correlation
    And a mismatch fails with a concise message naming the pull-request issue and evaluated spec directory

  # Added by issue #143
  Scenario: Relevant changed files map to planned or verified work
    Given a pull request changes non-trivial source, script, skill, template, or reference files
    When the contribution gate classifies changed paths and evaluates task and verification evidence
    Then every relevant path maps through an exact normalized path, an explicit containing-directory prefix, or path-specific behavior under test
    And evidence-only artifacts cannot stand in for unrelated implementation paths
    And missing mappings fail with a concise list of unmatched relevant paths

  # Added by issue #143
  Scenario: Verification evidence is specific
    Given a pull request states that tests or verification were run
    When the contribution gate evaluates the current verification section and committed verification artifacts
    Then generic keywords alone are insufficient
    And a command with an outcome, a non-empty report, an acceptance-criterion result, or a changed-path-specific result satisfies verification
    And quoted historical text outside the current evidence source does not satisfy verification

  # Added by issue #143
  Scenario: Explicit exceptions preserve low-friction workflows
    Given a pull request declares either "SDLC-Exception: docs-only" with a non-empty rationale or a correlated issue labelled "spike"
    And its changed paths are limited to artifacts allowed by that exception
    When the contribution gate validates the exception and complete changed-path set
    Then it applies the documented reduced evidence contract
    And issue linkage, steering presence, guide discoverability, and all non-exempt checks still apply
    And source, script, skill, template, or reference changes invalidate the exception with actionable remediation
